    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d568">

                <pb facs="0625" n="521" xml:id="pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.124/322.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-12-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 14, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A contract was signed today in Quito between the Government of Ecuador and James
                    W. McCrosky [sic] representing J. G. White and Company, Limited, of London, for
                    the sanitation works of Guayaquil; the amount involved is about $10,000,000.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
